# Native operator app (primary)

**Operator work is native-only (`rinse-mobile/`).** Do not ask whether to implement on PWA.

`rinse-api` is the **Next.js API + customer web** (book, portal, admin) — not an operator UI target. Do not rebuild the legacy operator PWA screens there.

## Default workflow

1. **Build in `rinse-mobile/`** — routes in `app/`, UI in `src/components/`, tokens in `src/theme/tokens.ts`.
2. **Reuse shared logic** — `@rinse/core` (`packages/core`), existing native lib patterns, `EXPO_PUBLIC_APP_API_URL` for backend APIs.
3. **API changes** — only in `rinse-api` when the native app or customer book/portal needs a server change (explicit or clearly required).

## RN Web pitfalls (already hit in this project)

- `ScrollView`: put `alignItems` / `gap` / `flexDirection` on **`contentContainerStyle`**, not `style`.
- `Pressable` + `accessibilityRole="button"` on web → `<button>` UA styles. Use `webPressableReset` (full-width rows) or `webInlinePressableReset` (pills/chips).
- Hidden Expo tabs stay mounted — reset list filters/stage when screen regains focus on tab focus.

## Do not

- Ask "PWA or native?" for operator features — **native only**.
- Mix client-light booking/portal tokens into operator native screens.
- Recreate operator jobs/clients/settings shells inside `rinse-api`.
